# Who reviews what.
#
# The point of this file: each team owns its own content directory, so teams
# publish their own updates without waiting on a central reviewer. The last
# matching rule wins, so the catch-all goes first and the specific rules follow.
#
# For it to mean anything, protect the default branch in Settings → Branches
# with "Require a pull request before merging" and "Require review from Code
# Owners". Without that, this file is only a suggestion.
#
# Replace the handles below with your own teams — these are the demo ones and
# they do not exist. See docs/adopting.md.

# The site itself — code, config, workflows, docs.
*                                           @example-org/platform-maintainers

# Team definitions and streamlines, owned by the teams they describe.
/content/teams/devops.yaml                  @example-org/devops
/content/streamlines/devops/                @example-org/devops

/content/teams/developer-experience.yaml    @example-org/developer-experience
/content/streamlines/developer-experience/  @example-org/developer-experience

/content/teams/ai-platform.yaml             @example-org/ai-platform
/content/streamlines/ai-platform/           @example-org/ai-platform

/content/teams/internal-tools.yaml          @example-org/internal-tools
/content/streamlines/internal-tools/        @example-org/internal-tools

# Adding a team is two lines here and one file in content/teams/.
